.docname {Telemetry Ingestion}
.include {docs}

.glossary
    | Word | Meaning | Example |
    |---|---|---|
    | Sensor | A device connected to a room | Thermometer `T-204` in Lab 2 |
    | Metric | A kind of thing we measure | Temperature |
    | Reading | One value from one room at one moment | Lab 2, 14:05, 27 °C |
    | Limit | The range a metric should stay in | 18 to 26 °C |
    | Limit Set | All the limits of one building | Science Hall's limits |
    | Breach | The time a room spends outside a limit | Lab 2, from 14:05 to 14:20 |
    | Window | A time range for looking at history | Last week |
    | Building Ready | News that a new building can be used | Science Hall is ready |

**Question:** what is happening in each room, and is it OK? **Kind:** Core. **Needs:** [Building Management](domain-buildings.qd), a reading needs a room.

Turns noise from devices into facts the platform can trust.

---

## In the real world

Lab 2 has a thermometer. Every few seconds it says a number.

- Some numbers are garbage, or come from a device nobody connected.
- Good numbers must be kept: after an incident, people ask what really happened.
- A number means little alone. 27 °C is fine in a corridor and bad in a server room.

So three jobs: **check** it, **keep** it, **judge** it.

---

## The model

.mermaid
    classDiagram
        class Sensor {
            name
            room
        }
        class Reading {
            room
            metric
            time
            value
        }
        class LimitSet {
            building
            buildingLimits
            roomLimits
        }
        class Limit {
            metric
            min
            max
        }
        class Breach {
            room
            metric
            startedAt
            endedAt
        }
        LimitSet "1" *-- "many" Limit
        Reading "many" ..> "1" Sensor : comes from
        Breach "1" ..> "1" Limit : broke

---

## A reading's path

.mermaid
    flowchart TD
        A["Reading arrives"] --> B{"Sensor connected?"}
        B -- no --> X["Rejected, with the reason"]
        B -- yes --> C{"Values make sense?"}
        C -- no --> X
        C -- yes --> D["Recorded"]
        D --> E["News: Reading Recorded"]
        D --> F{"Inside the limit?"}
        F -- "yes, and a breach was open" --> G["News: Breach Ended"]
        F -- "no, and no breach was open" --> H["News: Breach Started"]
        F -- "no change" --> I["Nothing else"]

Rejected readings never enter the platform. The sender is told why, so a broken device can be found.

---

## Which limit applies?

The room's own limit wins. Otherwise the building's.

| Room | Own limit | Building limit | Limit used | Reading | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Lab 2 | 18 to 26 | 16 to 28 | 18 to 26 | 27 | Breach |
| Corridor | none | 16 to 28 | 16 to 28 | 27 | OK |

A building has exactly one Limit Set. A new one replaces the old, so nobody asks which limit was active.

---

## One breach, many readings

A breach is a period, not a reading. This is what makes "one problem, one alert" true.

| Time | Value | Limit 18 to 26 | Breach | News |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 14:00 | 25 | Inside | None | |
| 14:05 | 27 | Above | Starts | Breach Started |
| 14:10 | 27.5 | Above | Still open | |
| 14:15 | 26.5 | Above | Still open | |
| 14:20 | 25 | Inside | Ends | Breach Ended |

.mermaid
    stateDiagram-v2
        Inside --> Outside: reading breaks the limit
        Outside --> Outside: still breaking it
        Outside --> Inside: reading is back in range

**Why here, and not in Alerting?** Whether 27 °C is bad depends on the room, and that is this domain's knowledge. Who hears about it is about people. That is Alerting's.

---

## Rules

1. Only a connected Sensor is listened to. Disconnect it and its next reading is rejected.
2. A Reading is never changed or deleted. A correction is a new Reading.
3. A Reading says which building, which room, and when. Missing one means rejected.
4. Each Metric has a name and a unit.

---

## How a metric describes itself

```text
name:  Temperature
unit:  °C
```

[Telemetry Distribution](domain-distribution.qd) collects these into its catalog. Describe Noise tomorrow and people can pick it right away.

---

## Looking back

History comes from recorded readings.

```text
Lab 2, temperature, Monday, average over the day
Readings:  22, 24, 27, 23
Average:   24 °C
```

---

## What leaves this domain

| What | How | To whom |
|---|---|---|
| Reading Recorded | News | Distribution |
| Breach Started | News | Alerting, Distribution |
| Breach Ended | News | Distribution |
| Metric descriptions | Shared list | Distribution |
| Current values and limits | Answer to a question | Knowledge & Assistance |

---

## Open questions

- A silent sensor: is no reading for an hour a problem? There is no story yet.
- A limit changes during a breach: judged again at the next reading?
- What are the starting limits for a new building?
